## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses your ability to align cost, risk, and velocity in a multi-team, multi-region environment with shared data platform infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- FinOps and cost governance in cloud-native environments
- SLOs/SLIs and error budget policies
- Multi-tenancy isolation and privacy controls
- Budgeting, chargeback, and ownership models
- Incident costing and blameless postmortems
- Experiments to validate operational readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Tagging for cost ownership
function tagResource(resource, owner, project) {
  return {
    ...resource,
    tags: {
      owner: owner,
      project: project,
      costCenter: getCostCenter(owner),
      environment: process.env.ENV
    }
  };
}
```
